From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: Drop nonexistent ccu-sun60i-a733-cpupll object

The A733 CPU PLL support is part of ccu-sun60i-a733.c. The Makefile
references a separate ccu-sun60i-a733-cpupll.o object that does not
exist, which breaks the build:

  make[5]: *** No rule to make target
  'drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpupll.o'

Remove the stray Makefile entry.

Signed-off-by: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile
@@ -36,5 +36,4 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN55I_A523_CCU)	+= sun55i-a523-ccu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN55I_A523_CCU)	+= ccu-sun60i-a733.o
-obj-$(CONFIG_SUN55I_A523_CCU)	+= ccu-sun60i-a733-cpupll.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN55I_A523_MCU_CCU)	+= sun55i-a523-mcu-ccu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN55I_A523_R_CCU)	+= sun55i-a523-r-ccu.o
